  [1mWhat removing it actually does:[0m [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m is the only gate on [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m ([38;5;153mserver.js:7[39m). Drop it and the route
  serves revenue data to any unauthenticated request that reaches the process — not just the dashboard script.
  "Internal" is a network claim, not an enforcement: nothing in this repo restricts who can reach the listener. If the
  service is behind a corporate LB, a VPN, or a shared cluster, every other tenant on that network becomes an authorized
  caller. And [38;5;153m/admin/*[39m is exactly the prefix that gets scanned once anything is accidentally exposed.

  It's one line to remove and one line to restore, but the window between those two is unauthenticated financial data.

